WEBVTT

00:36:55.420 --> 00:37:00.006
The Greek roots of nostalgia
translate to "return" and "pain."

00:37:00.030 --> 00:37:01.696
The literal definition is:

00:37:01.720 --> 00:37:04.796
the pain of being unable
to return to the past.

00:37:04.820 --> 00:37:06.306
But here's the strange thing:

00:37:06.330 --> 00:37:07.823
that's not how it feels.

00:37:08.920 --> 00:37:12.053
After people are randomly assigned
to reflect on a nostalgic event

00:37:12.077 --> 00:37:13.235
in their lives,

00:37:13.259 --> 00:37:15.196
they end up feeling happier.

00:37:15.220 --> 00:37:17.554
They have a stronger sense
of connection to others

00:37:17.578 --> 00:37:20.396
and become more willing
to give and seek help.

00:37:20.420 --> 00:37:23.220
They gain a deeper sense
of meaning and purpose in life.

00:37:24.190 --> 00:37:26.776
Think about a nostalgic
event in your life,

00:37:26.800 --> 00:37:28.657
something you had before the pandemic

00:37:28.681 --> 00:37:30.266
but no longer do,